From 8840ed16b85cfddf46a391dd5770df7cc3c8fd15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:28:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pwa): fail-closed service worker; honest session wording
 (R6)

Incremental patch after Build 69 baseline + R4 + R5. Draft; not deployed.
- sw.js: never intercepts auth/recovery/API/cross-origin/credentialed requests;
  allow-listed public static assets only; offline page instead of cached '/'
- activate removes legacy cliniverse-* caches; register-sw.js purges at launch,
  registers reliably after hydration, never registers from /reset-password
- /sw.js and /register-sw.js served no-store
- reset page wording distinguishes revoked refresh tokens from live access tokens
- type=recovery documented as a routing hint; simulated-vs-live evidence relabelled
- tests: SW policy suite on the real worker file; real-Chromium controlling-SW script

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
